<title>UK: Alliance average 2nd auction price 551p/shr.</title>
<headline>Alliance average 2nd auction price 551p/shr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banking and mortgage group Alliance &amp; Leicester, which floated on Monday, said on Tuesday that the average price of shares at its second auction of free shares by members was 551.00729 pence per share.</p>
<p>The average bid price of the first auction of free shares was 522.07814 pence a share.  </p>
<p>Alliance said 52.36 million shares were auctioned off at prices ranging between 534p and 575p.</p>
<p>The auction, which took place after close of Monday's trade, was the second in three auctions of free shares in the former building society.</p>
<p>A total of about 157 million shares are on offer after almost 27 percent of Alliance members opted to sell their free share allocation.</p>
<p>The third auction, of another 52.36 million shares, will take place on Tuesday between 1630 (1530 GMT) and 1830 (1730 GMT).</p>
<p>Alliance closed at 566 1/2 p on Monday, its first trading day, but had fallen 23 p to 543 1/2 p in early Tuesday morning trade.</p>
<p>--Arindam Nag, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
